From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 09:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] x11: The depth limits reach every declared child window

s52-0001 writes _KDE_NET_WM_STEREO_DEPTH_LIMITS on the window that declares
stereo content. A program whose 3D area is a child window (every Qt, GLX or
Mesa program that lists the child in _KDE_NET_WM_STEREO_CONTENT_CHILDREN, the
route stereo-window-3d-area describes) declares on the child and not on its
top level, so the property never reached the window the program looks at and
libstereo-declare answered -ENODATA ("offered, not delivered") for it.

X11Window::updateStereoDepthLimits() now writes the two values on each child
KWin tracks (X11StereoChildren) that holds its own stereo content, at the same
moments as for the window: at the declaration, at every change of the limits or
of the output, and when the list of children changes. X11StereoChildren::unwatch
deletes the property when the child leaves the list or the window goes, and the
declaration leaving the child deletes it too. The top level keeps its own rule.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 via Claude Code
---
--- a/src/x11stereochildren.h
+++ b/src/x11stereochildren.h
@@ -66,6 +66,10 @@
     // the child's own _KDE_NET_WM_STEREO_CONTENT_ONE_VIEW_SIZE: the size one view is shown at,
     // empty when the child declares none
     QSizeF oneViewSize;
+    // the values last written to the child's _KDE_NET_WM_STEREO_DEPTH_LIMITS: sunk and popped as
+    // 24.8 fixed point, as X11Window::updateStereoDepthLimits() writes them for a window
+    bool depthLimitsWritten = false;
+    uint32_t depthLimits[2] = {0, 0};
 
     // The child's place in the X11 window as the scene shows it, in this order: its declared
     // place (_KDE_NET_WM_STEREO_CONTENT_CHILD_PLACE); else, when it holds stereo content and
--- a/src/x11stereochildren.cpp
+++ b/src/x11stereochildren.cpp
@@ -191,6 +191,11 @@
 void X11StereoChildren::unwatch(X11StereoChild *child)
 {
     xcb_connection_t *connection = kwinApp()->x11Connection();
+    // the depth limits KWin wrote on the child go with the declaration
+    if (child->depthLimitsWritten) {
+        child->depthLimitsWritten = false;
+        xcb_discard_reply(connection, xcb_delete_property_checked(connection, child->window, atoms->kde_net_wm_stereo_depth_limits).sequence);
+    }
     // the child may be gone already, with its X11 window destroyed: that is no error to report
     xcb_discard_reply(connection, xcb_composite_unredirect_window_checked(connection, child->window, XCB_COMPOSITE_REDIRECT_MANUAL).sequence);
     if (Xcb::Extensions::self()->isShapeAvailable()) {
--- a/src/x11window.cpp
